{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implement a dynamic ModuleRegistry service interface (with an in-memory default implementation) that supports runtime registration/unregistration of modules; refactor the existing hard-coded ModuleRegistryPopulator to delegate to this service so newly contributed modules are immediately visible in the registry (U2).",
    "Expose module upload/registration through a REST API (POST/DELETE on a module resource, e.g., /modules) that accepts module coordinates (Maven group:artifact:version) and/or a resolvable URI; artifacts are resolved through the project's existing Maven resolution infrastructure rather than hosting binary uploads on the server (U1).",
    "Implement shell commands (e.g., 'module register'/'module upload') as thin clients that invoke the new REST API, reusing the existing shell-to-REST communication layer (U1).",
    "Migrate each Spring XD module to the Spring Cloud Stream programming model: @EnableBinding with Source/Sink channels, Spring Boot auto-configuration classes, and @ConfigurationProperties option classes with whitelisted properties (U3-U8).",
    "Structure each migrated module as a standalone Maven project in the target repository (spring-cloud-stream-modules for jms, mail, mongo; spring-cloud-stream for mqtt, reactor-ip, stdout) with its own build descriptor.",
    "Use JUnit 5 + Mockito for unit tests and embedded/lightweight brokers or servers for integration tests (embedded ActiveMQ for JMS, GreenMail or stub SMTP for mail, embedded MongoDB for mongo, embedded Mosquitto/broker stub for MQTT, local TCP/UDP sockets for reactor-ip).",
    "Baseline technology stack: Java 17, Spring Framework 6 / Spring Boot 3, consistent with the specification's stated minimum requirements.",
    "All development tasks (implementation, testing, documentation, build/CI configuration) are performed by a single developer, consistent with the assignment."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "'Upload custom modules' means registering a module's Maven coordinates or URI with the data flow server via shell/REST so it becomes usable in stream/task definitions; no server-side binary artifact repository or file-storage subsystem is required.",
    "The module registry keeps registrations in memory (matching the behavior of the initial implementation); persistence of registrations across server restarts is out of scope for this increment.",
    "Each XD module migration includes: porting the production code, adapting it to the Spring Cloud Stream binder model, creating option/properties classes, unit tests, integration tests, and Maven project scaffolding in the target repository.",
    "The six modules to migrate (jms, mail, mongo, mqtt, reactor-ip, stdout) exist in the Spring XD codebase and are functionally stable, so no new feature design is needed, only porting and adaptation.",
    "s-c-s-m refers to the spring-cloud-stream-modules repository and s-c-s to the spring-cloud-stream repository.",
    "The developer is experienced with Spring, Spring XD, and Spring Cloud Stream/Data Flow internals, so no significant learning-curve allowance is included.",
    "Estimates cover development effort only (design, coding, testing, documentation, CI setup); they exclude release management, production deployment, and post-release support.",
    "Code review, where applicable, is lightweight self-review performed within the implementation activities.",
    "Reasonable test coverage (unit plus integration) is required for all deliverables; no separate QA team is involved."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-01",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and solution design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze user stories U1-U8, review the existing ModuleRegistryPopulator and XD module code, and produce the design for the dynamic module registry, the module upload REST/shell interfaces, and the module migration approach (Spring Cloud Stream model, configuration properties, testing strategy).",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-02",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Implement dynamic module registry",
      "activity_description": "Implement the ModuleRegistry service supporting runtime registration/unregistration with immediate visibility, and refactor the hard-coded bootstrap populator to delegate to it so contributed modules instantly appear in the registry.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-03",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Module registry unit tests",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests covering registration, unregistration, duplicate handling, lookup, and immediate reflection of changes in stream/task definition resolution.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-04",
      "activity_name": "U1 - REST API for module upload/registration",
      "activity_description": "Implement the REST controller, request/response DTOs, validation, error handling, and wiring to the dynamic registry and Maven artifact resolution for uploading/registering custom modules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-05",
      "activity_name": "U1 - REST API integration tests",
      "activity_description": "Write integration tests for the upload/registration endpoints, including success, validation failure, and unresolvable-coordinate scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-06",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Shell commands for module upload/registration",
      "activity_description": "Implement shell commands (e.g., module register/upload/list/unregister) that invoke the new REST API, including command options, help text, and result formatting.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-07",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Shell command tests",
      "activity_description": "Write tests for the new shell commands covering argument parsing, REST interaction, and output rendering.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-08",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Migrate jms module to spring-cloud-stream-modules",
      "activity_description": "Port the JMS module from Spring XD to the Spring Cloud Stream source model: code migration, auto-configuration, properties classes, Maven project setup, and unit/integration tests with an embedded broker.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-09",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Migrate mail module to spring-cloud-stream-modules",
      "activity_description": "Port the mail module from Spring XD to the Spring Cloud Stream source model, including auto-configuration, properties, project setup, and tests with a stub/embedded mail server.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-10",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Migrate mongo module to spring-cloud-stream-modules",
      "activity_description": "Port the mongo module from Spring XD to the Spring Cloud Stream source model, including auto-configuration, properties, project setup, and tests against embedded MongoDB.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-11",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Migrate mqtt module to spring-cloud-stream",
      "activity_description": "Port the mqtt module from Spring XD to the Spring Cloud Stream source model, including auto-configuration, properties, project setup, and tests with an embedded/stub MQTT broker.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-12",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Migrate reactor-ip module to spring-cloud-stream",
      "activity_description": "Port the reactor-based TCP/UDP IP module from Spring XD to the Spring Cloud Stream source model, adapting reactive connection handling, auto-configuration, properties, project setup, and socket-level integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-13",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Migrate stdout module to spring-cloud-stream",
      "activity_description": "Port the simple stdout module from Spring XD to the Spring Cloud Stream model, including minimal auto-configuration, project setup, and tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-14",
      "activity_name": "Build and CI configuration for new modules and endpoints",
      "activity_description": "Configure parent POMs, module build descriptors, dependency management, and continuous-integration build definitions for the migrated modules and the updated data flow components.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-15",
      "activity_name": "Documentation updates",
      "activity_description": "Update reference documentation and READMEs: dynamic registry behavior, module upload via REST/shell usage examples, and per-module configuration property documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-16",
      "activity_name": "End-to-end integration verification and defect fixing",
      "activity_description": "Perform end-to-end verification: register an uploaded custom module via shell and REST, confirm immediate registry visibility, and build streaming pipelines using each migrated module; fix defects found.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 300
  }
}
